# Python ML Standards

## Stack (mandatory)

Python 3.11+, PyTorch, scikit-learn, MLflow, DVC, Pandas, NumPy, Ruff, Pytest, Poetry/uv.

## Code

- Type hints + Google docstrings on public APIs
- Functions ≤ 20 lines; SOLID; Factory for models, Strategy for preprocessors
- Fixed seeds via `src/training/seeds.py`; log config to MLflow

## Dependencies

Only use packages in `.cursor/libs/allowed-libs.md`. No TensorFlow unless explicitly approved.

## Layout

`src/domain`, `src/data`, `src/features`, `src/models`, `src/training`, `src/evaluation`, `src/serving`

## Prohibited

Node.js tooling, notebooks as production training path, hardcoded secrets, raw MovieLens in Git.
